### Notification System — Docker demo requests
### Prereq: docker compose up --build
### All requests go through nginx (localhost:8080), which load-balances across
### notification-service-1 and notification-service-2.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Health check (either service instance behind nginx)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health


### Send an email notification
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/notifications/email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": [{ "userId": 1 }],
  "from": { "email": "no-reply@example.com" },
  "subject": "Welcome to the platform",
  "content": [{ "type": "text/plain", "value": "Hi there, thanks for signing up!" }]
}


### Send an SMS notification
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/notifications/sms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": [{ "userId": 1 }],
  "content": [{ "type": "text/plain", "value": "Your verification code is 123456" }]
}


### Send a push notification
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/notifications/push
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": [{ "userId": 1 }],
  "subject": "New message",
  "content": [{ "type": "text/plain", "value": "You have a new message waiting" }]
}


### Validation error — empty recipient list (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/notifications/email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": [],
  "from": { "email": "no-reply@example.com" },
  "subject": "Missing recipients",
  "content": [{ "type": "text/plain", "value": "This should fail validation" }]
}
